<title>ITALY: Italy ERM re-entry bid &quot;a matter of weeks&quot; - Ciampi.</title>
<headline>Italy ERM re-entry bid &quot;a matter of weeks&quot; - Ciampi.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1996-11-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian government will ask to put the lira back into the European exchange rate mechanism (ERM) in the coming weeks, Treasury Minister Carlo Azeglio Ciampi said in an interview with L'Unita newspaper.</p>
<p>Asked when the lira would return to the ERM, Ciampi replied:</p>
<p>&quot;We will ask about the ERM re-entry shortly. The return is tied to the approval of the budget and it will be a government decision. It is a question of weeks.&quot;</p>
</text>
